{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "realtime/each-session-of-a-channel-fires-its-own-audio-levels-once-per-100-ms",
  "title": "Two sessions of one realtime channel, fed at the same instants, each fire their own input and output levels, at most one per 100 ms",
  "rules": [
    "§12.5",
    "§9.2"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-12.5-030"
  ],
  "requires_features": [
    "realtime"
  ],
  "notes": "What the voice scenarios of RK-12.5-030 leave out: the limit per session on a realtime voice channel. Two sessions of the one channel, in two rooms, are each handed two caller frames and two chunks of the model's audio at 0, 60, 120, 180 and 240 ms of the virtual clock, at the same instants: unthrottled, ten levels a session and a direction. Each session fires its own, at 0, 120 and 240 ms, whatever the other sent: a throttle the channel's sessions share leaves the second session none, a 50 ms interval fires five, a 200 ms one two. The voice scenarios pin the interval itself; the idle wait after each instant lets the model's audio reach the transport at that instant's reading.",
